= Balancing Chemical Equations

*Grade 9 Chemistry Worksheet*

Name: #line(length: 6cm) Date: #line(length: 3cm)

== Instructions

Balance each chemical equation by placing whole-number coefficients in front of the formulas. Do not change any subscripts. Check that the number of atoms of every element is the same on both sides. Problems get harder as you go. Show your counting in the space provided.

== Part A: Easy

*1.* $"H"_2 + "O"_2 -> "H"_2"O"$

#v(2em)

*2.* $"Na" + "Cl"_2 -> "NaCl"$

#v(2em)

*3.* $"Mg" + "HCl" -> "MgCl"_2 + "H"_2$

#v(2em)

== Part B: Medium

*4.* $"CH"_4 + "O"_2 -> "CO"_2 + "H"_2"O"$

#v(2em)

*5.* $"Al" + "O"_2 -> "Al"_2"O"_3$

#v(2em)

*6.* $"Fe" + "H"_2"O" -> "Fe"_3"O"_4 + "H"_2$

#v(2em)

== Part C: Hard

*7.* $"C"_3"H"_8 + "O"_2 -> "CO"_2 + "H"_2"O"$

#v(2em)

*8.* $"Ca"("OH")_2 + "H"_3"PO"_4 -> "Ca"_3("PO"_4)_2 + "H"_2"O"$

#v(2em)

*9.* $"KMnO"_4 + "HCl" -> "KCl" + "MnCl"_2 + "H"_2"O" + "Cl"_2$

Hint: Balance the metals first, then oxygen, then hydrogen, and balance chlorine last.

#v(2em)

*10.* $"Cu" + "HNO"_3 -> "Cu"("NO"_3)_2 + "NO" + "H"_2"O"$

Hint: Nitrogen appears in three places. Balance the copper and the nitrate group before hydrogen and oxygen.

#v(2em)

